# A save that fails (the disk is full, or the file is read-only) leaves the file on the disk as it was and the document unsaved; a retry on a disk with room saves.
@file "FULL.TXT" "the original words"
@file "LOCKED.TXT" "the locked words"
@full FULL.TXT
@locked LOCKED.TXT
cmd Open
expect file Open
choose "FULL.TXT"
type "!"
cmd Save
dump
cmd Open
expect ask default Yes
answer No
expect file Open
choose "LOCKED.TXT"
type "?"
cmd Save
dump
